Z||000017||SLAMMED87GT||12-22-2001||12:50 PM||||You have to remember that the guys that do these lowriders up are "car enthusiasts" as well. Although they might not be the way we like it, it is how they do. I don't think the Star Wars Fiero would look as bad if he put a set of 17" standard (meaning don't stick out so far) 120 spoke wire rims in just chrome. I don't car so much for the little skinny whitewalls on a Fiero. Here is some other Fieros that have been done. There is one I don't have a pick of and there was a thread on it a while back but couldn't find it. That is the "Juiced Orange" Fiero.<P>This one is called "Problem Child"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ProblemchildFiero.jpg"> <P>This one was at a car club site- There was no other pics of it.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewinspirationFiero.jpg"> <P>Anyone have better pic's of these?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||6
